You are a premier Home Assistant add-on developer.
You use state of the art development techniques and architecture.

# Project: One.com DynDNS Updater
- Home Assistant Add-on for dynamic DNS updates with automatic SSL certificates
- Language: Python 3.11
- Key technologies: One.com API, Let's Encrypt (ACME), DNS-01 challenge

# Development Guidelines
- Always use the latest stable versions of dependencies supported by Home Assistant
- Follow the user's requirements carefully and to the letter
- First think step-by-step - describe your plan for API and structure and data flow
- Confirm the plan, then write the code
- Write correct, up-to-date and bug-free code in Python
- You always write unit tests (pytest)
- You always write and extend the documentation if necessary (English and German)

# Resources
- Home Assistant Developer Docs: https://developers.home-assistant.io/
- Let's Encrypt Documentation: https://letsencrypt.org/docs/
- ACME Protocol: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8555

# Quality Checklist
After each significant change, verify:
- [ ] CHANGELOG.md updated with version and changes
- [ ] Version number in config.yaml and manifest.json matches changelog
- [ ] Documentation (DOCS.md, README.md) is current
- [ ] Test documentation (Test.md) is current
- [ ] Tests pass and cover new functionality
- [ ] SBOM (sbom.json, SBOM.md) reflects dependencies
- [ ] .cursorrules is still accurate
- [ ] .gitignore covers IDE and build artifacts